WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.250
Private payments, parallel blocks, post-quantum signatures: Bitcoin, Kaspa and Monero do not offer all three.

2
00:00:08.777 --> 00:00:14.563
With Bitcoin, anyone can trace which addresses were used and which amounts were transferred.

3
00:00:14.563 --> 00:00:17.347
The ledger does not name the key holders.

4
00:00:17.347 --> 00:00:24.070
The Phexora Cash design aims for private payments by default, with proof of one payment whenever you choose.

5
00:00:24.543 --> 00:00:28.525
Kaspa orders blocks in parallel for high layer-one throughput.

6
00:00:28.525 --> 00:00:33.216
A standard payment still shows its inputs, outputs and amounts.

7
00:00:33.216 --> 00:00:43.700
The Phexora Cash design pairs parallel blocks with private payments and targets at least 1,000 accepted private payments per second on layer one for 24 hours.

8
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:52.081
Monero hides the amount and the recipient, obscures the source, and lets you prove one payment to someone you choose.

9
00:00:52.081 --> 00:00:58.576
Its standard signatures rely on classical elliptic curves, and its blocks form a single chain.

10
00:00:58.576 --> 00:01:06.740
The Phexora Cash design targets at least 128 bits of post-quantum security across the whole system, and parallel blocks.

11
00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:10.751
This is the research question behind Phexora Cash.

12
00:01:10.751 --> 00:01:16.910
Can one design combine all three, and also protect the origin of a payment from network observers?

13
00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:27.989
Side by side, you see that standard payments are public on Bitcoin and Kaspa, Bitcoin and Monero use a single chain, and all three rely on classical signatures.

14
00:01:27.989 --> 00:01:33.100
The Phexora Cash column lists design targets, and no conformant network exists.

15
00:01:33.664 --> 00:01:43.290
Release also requires independent validation and recovery, miners who can choose their own transactions, and a separate review of long-term security funding.

16
00:01:43.817 --> 00:01:50.430
You can read the design, the verification plan and the proposed feasibility study at cash.phexora.ai.
